  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe last slice of #163, after PR #222 (app seams: save/open/post/generate/commands) and PR #969 (app library eprintln!s and the budget-refusal events). With this, no diagnostic in the library or UI crates bypasses the one `tracing` subscriber any more.\n\n- **Library crates** (`camcraft-cl`, `-geometry`, `-motion`, `-sim`, `-tools`): every non-test `eprintln!` is now a `tracing` event - refusals and fallbacks at `warn` (refused move/builder axis or C angle; multi-axis moves held vertical or radial, a rotary start on the axis, a degenerate drive curve skipped; a non-finite sim path left out or move held still; the dual iso-surface falling back to marching tetrahedra; a missing starter tool catalog), the opt-in `CAMCRAFT_PROFILE_PROJECTION` profile lines at `info`. The text of each line is unchanged.\n- **Standalone bins** (`camcraft-cl`, `-geometry`, `-motion`, `-sim`, `-tools`): each installs a stderr subscriber with the app's filter rule (`CAMCRAFT_LOG`, else `RUST_LOG`, else `info`), so the converted library warnings still reach their terminal. Their own `println!` reports and usage errors are the CLI's answer and stay as they are.\n- **UI**: the `diag` seam (#31) now emits `tracing` events natively (target `camcraft_ui`, `warn`/`info`) instead of `eprintln!`/`println!`; wasm32 still goes to the browser console. The native window (`shell_window.rs`, `shell_window/frame.rs`), GPU bring-up (`gpu_init.rs`), Cmd+Q hook (`os_quit.rs`) and the headless proof (`shell.rs`) now speak through the seam, so the law test's allow-list shrinks to the seam and test-only code (`gpu.rs`'s test module, `headless_gpu.rs`'s `device_for_test`, whose \"SKIPPED - NOT a pass\" line must show in a test run with no subscriber).\n\n**Dependencies.** No new crate: `tracing` and `tracing-subscriber` are already workspace dependencies (root `Cargo.toml`, since PR #222) and in `Cargo.lock`; this PR adds `{ workspace = true }` lines for them to the five library crates and `tracing` (plus `tracing-subscriber` as a dev-dependency) to `camcraft-ui`. `Cargo.lock` gains only those dependency edges. No `camcraft-*` edge is added. Decision record: `docs/decisions/163-tracing-libs.md`.\n\nThe issue's \"Done means\" is now covered across the three PRs: post writes name the file and result or why not (#222), a generation budget names its limit (#969, `a_budget_refusal_names_the_limit_that_fired_at_warn`), levels come from `CAMCRAFT_LOG`/`RUST_LOG` with a quiet `info` default (#222), and the library/UI prints that bypassed the filter are gone (this PR). No event was added inside a hot loop (the geometry profile lines stay behind their env var).\n\n## How tested\n\n- New pinning tests:\n  - `camcraft-cl` `tests/refusal_log.rs::a_refused_axis_or_angle_is_a_warning_under_the_cl_target` - a refused move axis, C angle and builder axis are each a `WARN` event under `camcraft_cl`, and a stricter filter silences them.\n  - `camcraft-ui` `diag::tests::diag_lines_are_tracing_events_at_their_level` - `diag_warn!`/`diag_info!` are `WARN`/`INFO` events under `camcraft_ui`, and a filter below them stays quiet.\n  - `camcraft-ui` `diag::tests::shared_ui_code_prints_only_through_the_diag_seam` (existing law, allow-list tightened).\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`; Cargo changes fall back to batch scope): green on every test step in 27.9 min (geometry, kernel, cl, tools, post, sim, motion, app, ui suites all ok). The clippy step fails only on the pre-existing `MIN_LABEL_PX is never used` in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/painted.rs:115` (upstream main, #2104, not touched here); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean, and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings -A dead_code` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The wasm32 build of the UI was not run (the diag wasm branch is unchanged).\n- The real GPU window and the Windows GUI-subsystem console were not launched by hand; the converted lines are the same text through the same seam.\n- Pre-existing, not from this PR: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` fails on upstream main at 780b0a25a with `constant MIN_LABEL_PX is never used` (painted.rs:115, after PR #2095). Filed as #2104 (P2).\n\nBranched from upstream/main 780b0a25a (the fork's own main is stale; this branch carries none of it).\n\nChangelog: Library and UI diagnostics (refusals, multi-axis and sim fallbacks, GPU bring-up, the Cmd+Q hook) now go through the same filtered terminal log as the app's (CAMCRAFT_LOG / RUST_LOG); the standalone camcraft-cl/-geometry/-motion/-sim/-tools tools print them too.\n\nProcess change: no\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #163\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n## Launch-terminal screenshots\n\nThese screenshots show real launches of the native `camcraft-ui` executable in an X11 terminal.\nThe command uses an invalid shell name. It exercises the warning in `crates/ui/src/diag.rs` without opening a GPU window.\n\nThe after executable comes from head `33cf46fbe02052c0f67fdb1ffbf22919c3fb1bf2`.\nThe before executable comes from that head with only the two native diagnostic calls restored to their pre-PR form.\nThose calls match `crates/ui/src/diag.rs` at baseline `780b0a25a40606dc3cc96f56ab0b2c8ecb1093e6`.\nThe temporary source changes were restored after capture. No executable or screenshot is in this PR branch.\n\nRun each executable with these commands:\n\n```sh\nCAMCRAFT_LOG=info ./camcraft-ui --ui legacy\nCAMCRAFT_LOG=off ./camcraft-ui --ui legacy\n```\n\nBefore: the terminal prints the plain refusal for both filters.\nAfter: the terminal shows the timestamp, `WARN` level and `camcraft_ui` target at `info`. The `off` filter suppresses the warning.\nBoth commands return exit code 2 in both versions.\n\nThe screenshots are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n![Before: plain diagnostic bypasses the filter](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/da945c1bf2c1225c326274280fbed9ac4104ec74/2110/before.png)\n\n![After: tracing warning obeys the filter](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/da945c1bf2c1225c326274280fbed9ac4104ec74/2110/after.png)\n\nThe existing pin is `diag::tests::diag_lines_are_tracing_events_at_their_level`.\nThe mutation check was RED with the two old print calls. The warning assertion failed.\nAfter restoration, the same pin was GREEN (1 passed, 0 failed).\n\nTouched-crate clippy was RED with `-D warnings`.\nIt reports the existing unused `MIN_LABEL_PX` constant at `crates/ui/src/egui_app/painted.rs:115`.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` completed in 53.3 minutes.\nCargo.lock changes selected the batch tests. All nine test steps were GREEN.\nThe gate was RED only at clippy, for the same existing `MIN_LABEL_PX` warning.\nNo unrelated source change was made.\n",
